       shares this one (`.hobby-frozen-overlay`, `.hobby-palm-base`,
       `.hobby-palm-80s`, `.hobby-monado`, `.hobby-monado-symbol`,
       `.hobby-fountain-image` below) — none of them set their own
       `height` either, so this single rule fixes all of them via the
       normal CSS cascade. */
    height: auto;
    /* New: explicit `aspect-ratio` too, on top of `height: auto`
       above. Every image sharing this class really is the same
       3840x2160 canvas (that's the whole point of the technique — see
       the top-of-file comment), so this is a separate concern from the
       squish bug `height: auto` fixed: <Image /> defaults to
       `loading="lazy"` for every one of these (nothing here passes an
       explicit `loading` prop), and Chrome specifically flags a lazy
