     cyan chromatic-aberration ghost flashes.

     v24 — per your feedback, that read as the water's SHAPE itself
     moving around, not a digital effect happening ON/INSIDE the water
     — an accurate read: v23's slices displaced the entire clipped
     water layer sideways, which shifts its silhouette against
     everything else on the front island, rather than confining the
     glitch to stay strictly within the water's own boundary. Back to
     `mask-image` (`--fountain-mask`, unchanged since v19 — the mask
     mechanism itself was never what failed in any of the earlier
     attempts) to pin the effect's outer edge exactly to the water's
     real silhouette and never let it move, and per your ask for
